    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17932" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτό-στολος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>self-sent, going</i> or
				<i>acting of oneself,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				496
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.585
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Jul.
			</span></i>): metaph. of Leander swimming, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Musae.
					255
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτόστολον ναυλοῦν</span> to let
			a ship <i>by private contract</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				572.41
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Myra</span>).</div>
